======================== Hot Shard Problem ========================

One shard receives disproportionately high traffic.
Celebrity user -> all traffic hits one shard

Problems:
uneven load
CPU bottleneck
storage imbalance
Fixes
better shard key
hashing
resharding
consistent hashing

======================== SQL Horizontal Partitioning Tradeoffs ========================
1. Joins Become Hard
Cross-shard joins are expensive.
Query Shard A
Query Shard B
Move data across network
Merge results

This becomes:
Distributed Join
not a normal local join anymore.

2. Transactions Become Complex
ACID across shards is difficult.
Requires:
2PC (Two-Phase Commit)
sagas
distributed coordination

3. Operational Complexity
resharding requires data movement
shard mapping management
routing logic in application

4. Limited Flexibility
Changing shard key later is extremely painful.
